{"name":"Groundbreaking","hex":"#7b6f60","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"groundbreaking","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Innovative; new, different; doing something that has never been done before."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The point at which construction begins, by digging into the ground.","A ceremony to mark the beginning of construction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groundbreaking"}],"entries":[{"title":"Groundbreaking","blocks":[{"text":"Groundbreaking, also known as cutting, sod-cutting, turning the first sod, turf-cutting, or a sod-turning ceremony, is a traditional ceremony in many cultures that celebrates the first day of construction for a building or other project. Such ceremonies are often attended by dignitaries such as politicians and business people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Hunts_Point_groundbreaking.jpg/330px-Hunts_Point_groundbreaking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groundbreaking","wikidata":"Q1068633"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg/330px-Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg/960px-Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg/330px-Staedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStaedel-spatenstich-2009-038.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Nikolaus-schweickart-ffm-009.jpg/120px-Nikolaus-schweickart-ffm-009.jpg?utm_s